  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contracting in Iowa totaled $1.4B in obligations in FY2026 to date. The state saw 19,617 awards with an average award size of $72.3K, and obligations fell 60.8% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in the state with $915M in obligations, followed by the Department of the Treasury with $175M and the Department of Agriculture with $105M. ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. is the top vendor with $312M in obligations, followed by DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC with $277M and PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. with $116M. Other major industry recipients include Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $286M and Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying at $116M. The FY21 through FY26 series shows obligations ranging from $2.5B in FY21 to $3.6B in FY25, with the most recent FY26 total at $1.4B. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date obligations. The figures above are contract obligations for the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
