        "body": "Obligations fell 60.8% year over year in FY2026 to date. Fiscal-year obligations moved from $3.6B in FY25 to $1.4B in FY26. The state recorded 19,617 awards in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $72.3K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal contracting in Iowa?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $915M in FY2026 to date. The Department of the Treasury follows with $175M and the Department of Agriculture with $105M. ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. is the top vendor with $312M, followed by DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC with $277M and PMX INDUSTRIES, INC. with $116M."
      }
    ]
